{
  "_comment": "Dual-execution mock-fidelity corpus (ADR 0049, T6). Each journey is replayed against BOTH the TS mock runtime (src/test/scenarios/fidelity.test.ts) and the real Rust AppState/storage layer (src-tauri/src/storage/tests/mock_fidelity.rs). Both must satisfy every assertion, so the hand-written mock runtime cannot silently drift from real backend behavior (ts-rs guarantees DTO shapes; this guarantees behavior). Journeys use only seed-free root entities (watchlists, companies) so no scenario seeding is needed; assertions are seed-independent (create/rename/delete then assert the effect, never absolute counts), and a created entity's id is captured and reused so the assertions hold regardless of each side's id-derivation scheme. Step grammar: command, input (the invoke args, with \"$name\" leaves substituted from captures), optional capture (stores result.id), expectField (result object superset), expectContains / expectAbsent (result array contains / does not contain an element matching the subset).",
  "journeys": [
    {
      "name": "watchlist create-list-rename-delete lifecycle",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_watchlist",
          "input": { "input": { "name": "Fidelity Watch", "description": null } },
          "capture": "wid",
          "expectField": { "name": "Fidelity Watch" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_watchlists",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "name": "Fidelity Watch" }
        },
        {
          "command": "rename_watchlist",
          "input": { "input": { "id": "$wid", "name": "Fidelity Renamed", "description": null } },
          "expectField": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_watchlists",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" },
          "expectAbsent": { "name": "Fidelity Watch" }
        },
        {
          "command": "delete_watchlist",
          "input": { "watchlistId": "$wid" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_watchlists",
          "input": {},
          "expectAbsent": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "company create-list-delete lifecycle with qualified ticker",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "FDLTY",
              "displayName": "Fidelity Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid",
          "expectField": { "ticker": "FDLTY", "qualifiedTicker": "GPW:FDLTY" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_companies",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "ticker": "FDLTY", "qualifiedTicker": "GPW:FDLTY" }
        },
        {
          "command": "delete_company",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_companies",
          "input": {},
          "expectAbsent": { "ticker": "FDLTY" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "cockpit layout save-list-rename-delete lifecycle",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "save_cockpit_layout",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "name": "Fidelity Cockpit",
              "panelsJson": "{\"panels\":[\"feed\"]}",
              "layoutJson": null,
              "dockviewVersion": "6.6.1"
            }
          },
          "capture": "lid",
          "expectField": { "name": "Fidelity Cockpit", "ordinal": 0 }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_cockpit_layouts",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "name": "Fidelity Cockpit" }
        },
        {
          "command": "rename_cockpit_layout",
          "input": { "input": { "id": "$lid", "name": "Fidelity Renamed" } },
          "expectField": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_cockpit_layouts",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" },
          "expectAbsent": { "name": "Fidelity Cockpit" }
        },
        {
          "command": "delete_cockpit_layout",
          "input": { "layoutId": "$lid" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_cockpit_layouts",
          "input": {},
          "expectAbsent": { "name": "Fidelity Renamed" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "autopilot trust-ladder set-get round-trip (ADR 0055)",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "AUTOP",
              "displayName": "Autopilot Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid"
        },
        {
          "command": "set_company_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid", "mode": "assist" } },
          "expectField": { "mode": "assist" }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_company_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid" } },
          "expectField": { "mode": "assist" }
        },
        {
          "command": "set_company_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid", "mode": "autopilot" } },
          "expectField": { "mode": "autopilot" }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_company_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid" } },
          "expectField": { "mode": "autopilot" }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_autopilot_runs",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid" } },
          "expectAbsent": { "status": "succeeded" }
        },
        {
          "command": "set_companies_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyIds": ["$cid"], "mode": "off" } }
        },
        {
          "command": "list_company_autopilot_modes",
          "input": {},
          "expectContains": { "mode": "off" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "qualitative criterion create + empty current-state read (ADR 0075)",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_quality_framework",
          "input": { "input": { "name": "Qual Fidelity", "description": null } },
          "capture": "fid",
          "expectField": { "name": "Qual Fidelity" }
        },
        {
          "command": "create_framework_criterion",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "frameworkId": "$fid",
              "label": "Wide moat",
              "expression": "",
              "weight": null,
              "partialBand": null,
              "kind": "qualitative",
              "assessmentGuidance": "Assess durable competitive advantage."
            }
          },
          "capture": "crit",
          "expectField": {
            "kind": "qualitative",
            "assessmentGuidance": "Assess durable competitive advantage.",
            "expression": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_qualitative_assessment",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "co_fidelity_qual", "frameworkId": "$fid" } },
          "expectAbsent": { "source": "agent" }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_qualitative_assessment_status",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "co_fidelity_qual", "frameworkId": "$fid" } },
          "expectField": { "status": "idle" }
        },
        {
          "command": "run_qualitative_assessment",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "co_fidelity_qual", "frameworkId": "$fid" } }
        },
        {
          "command": "rerun_qualitative_criterion",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "co_fidelity_qual", "frameworkId": "$fid", "criterionId": "$crit" } }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_qualitative_assessment",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "co_fidelity_qual", "frameworkId": "$fid" } },
          "expectAbsent": { "source": "agent" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "reclassify report documents is an idempotent no-op (ADR 0077 T1.4)",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "reclassify_report_documents",
          "input": {},
          "expectField": { "updated": 0 }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "fundamentals coverage assembles a period row from a fact (ADR 0077 T2.1)",
      "_comment": "Coverage is a computed read model returning an object (companyId + periods array), not an array, so the subset harness can only assert its invariant top-level field. expectField is NOT capture-substituted (only step input is), so the companyId is asserted as the deterministic derived id (company_{exchange}_{ticker}, identical on both sides — the same scheme the qualified-ticker journey relies on). Per-cell correctness — a period row with facts.total >= 1 and report null — is pinned by the Rust unit tests and the TS mock scenario tests; this step proves both dispatchers implement the command and key the DTO by the scoped company.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "COVRG",
              "displayName": "Coverage Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid"
        },
        {
          "command": "create_financial_period",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "companyId": "$cid",
              "fiscalYear": 2025,
              "periodType": "FY",
              "periodEndDate": null,
              "reportEvidenceRef": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "pid"
        },
        {
          "command": "create_financial_fact",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "companyId": "$cid",
              "periodId": "$pid",
              "definitionId": "kpidef_net_profit",
              "valueNumeric": "1000"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_fundamentals_coverage",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" },
          "expectField": { "companyId": "company_gpw_covrg" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "report documents view returns an empty rows array for a company with no documents (ADR 0077 Panel B)",
      "_comment": "The view is a computed read model returning an object (companyId + rows array). Report documents are seeded only through the network-bound fetch/backfill path (same rationale as the T2.1 coverage step), so the corpus exercises the empty case: a fresh company has no documents, so rows is []. The subset harness compares scalar fields (TS uses ===, so it cannot deep-compare the empty array), hence we assert the deterministic derived companyId — this proves both dispatchers implement the command and key the DTO by the scoped company. Per-row correctness (period fields, canonical ★) is pinned by the Rust unit tests in commands/report_documents_view.rs and the TS mock scenario tests.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "DOCVW",
              "displayName": "Docs View Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid"
        },
        {
          "command": "get_report_documents_view",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" },
          "expectField": { "companyId": "company_gpw_docvw" }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "history sweep starts a manual sweep and reports empty progress (ADR 0077 T3.2)",
      "_comment": "A history sweep enqueues extraction runs; run_history_sweep gates on mode != off (the UI disables the button in mode off), so the corpus opts the company into assist first. Report documents are seeded only through the network-bound fetch/backfill path (same rationale as the T2.1 coverage step), so the sweep runs over an empty company: it enqueues nothing, leaving runsTotal/runsDone/runsFailed at 0 — the stable scalars the subset harness pins. The returned sweep's trigger is the deterministic 'manual'. Per-run progress correctness is pinned by the Rust unit tests in commands/history_sweep.rs and the TS mock scenario tests.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "SWEEP",
              "displayName": "Sweep Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid"
        },
        {
          "command": "set_company_autopilot",
          "input": { "input": { "companyId": "$cid", "mode": "assist" } }
        },
        {
          "command": "run_history_sweep",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" },
          "expectField": { "trigger": "manual", "companyId": "company_gpw_sweep" }
        },
        {
          "command": "get_history_sweep_progress",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" },
          "expectField": { "runsTotal": 0, "runsDone": 0, "runsFailed": 0 }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "review queue lists no pending proposals for a company with no extractions (ADR 0077 T5.3b)",
      "_comment": "The F5 review-queue read model returns an array of pending proposals. KPI proposals are seeded only through the network-bound extraction-job path (same rationale as the T2.1 coverage step), so the corpus exercises the empty case: a fresh company has no jobs, so the array is []. expectAbsent asserts no returned item is a pending proposal — vacuously true over the empty array on BOTH dispatchers, proving each implements the command, returns an array, and keys it by the scoped company. Per-row correctness (period/document context, source_snippet passthrough, status filter) is pinned by the Rust unit test in storage/kpi_extraction.rs and the TS mock scenario tests.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "command": "create_company",
          "input": {
            "input": {
              "exchange": "GPW",
              "ticker": "RVIEW",
              "displayName": "Review Test S.A.",
              "isin": null,
              "cik": null,
              "lei": null
            }
          },
          "capture": "cid"
        },
        {
          "command": "list_pending_kpi_proposals",
          "input": { "companyId": "$cid" },
          "expectAbsent": { "status": "pending" }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
